cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this replication package, please cite it as below."
title: "NHANES Blood-Test Multi-Disease Screening: A Replication of EyeGuard7-Style Stacking Ensembles"
abstract: >-
  A full replication of the multi-cohort stacking-ensemble methodology described in
  "Large-scale screening of blinding eye diseases from routine blood tests" (EyeGuard7),
  applied to 41,333 NHANES participants across four survey cycles (2013-2014, 2015-2016,
  2017-2018, 2021-2023). The package includes the data pipeline, eight base learners with
  a logistic-regression meta-learner, exhaustive search over 255 base-learner subsets,
  recursive feature elimination to 12 features, internal plus external time-based
  validation, SHAP interpretability analysis, and trained model weights for seven
  diseases. Key findings include a consistent stacking gain over the best single learner
  (+0.0080 AUC on average), preserved performance after reduction to 12 features, and a
  quantified label-leakage inflation of +0.0708 AUC for diabetes when same-source
  diagnostic variables are used as features.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The NHANES Blood-Test Screening Replication Authors"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: MIT
